@page
@model Parley.Web.Pages.Projects.RegisterModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = $"Register an agent in {Model.Project}";
}

<h1>Register an agent in @Model.Project</h1>

<p>
    Prefer to point at a folder? <a href="/?tab=agents&amp;project=@Model.Project">Register from the agents page</a> instead.
    This page is for writing the file yourself. An agent's name comes from its launch configuration and nowhere else.
    No call can supply it, so a sender cannot forge the agent it claims to be. This page can only tell you what to write.
</p>

<h2>1. Name the agent in the repository</h2>

<p>Put this in <code>.mcp.json</code> at the root of the repository that will act as the agent:</p>

<pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "parley-@Model.Project": {
      "command": "parley-mcp",
      "env": {
        "PARLEY_AGENT": "&lt;a short name, lower case&gt;",
        "PARLEY_PROJECT": "@Model.Project"
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>

<p>
    A repository in several projects holds one entry for each, each under its own key. Leave an existing
    <code>parley</code> entry as it is.
</p>

<p>
    If this machine does not name the project, use <code>"PARLEY_BROKER": "@Model.Endpoint"</code> in place of
    <code>PARLEY_PROJECT</code>.
</p>

<p>
    What the repository owns is not written by hand. The agent reports it once it has registered, and you can
    review and change it under <a href="/Projects/Ownership?project=@Model.Project">Review ownership</a>.
</p>

<p>
    That file is usually tracked, so <strong>which branch is checked out decides whether the agent exists</strong>.
    On a branch without the entry the agent is absent, and nothing reports it. Put the entry on the
    branch everything else is cut from.
</p>

<h2>2. Open the repository</h2>

<p>Start a session in that repository. Attaching registers the agent.</p>

<h2>3. Confirm it worked</h2>

<p>
    Go to <a href="/?tab=agents&amp;project=@Model.Project">this project's agents</a>.
    The new name appears there once its session has attached. If it does not, the session's own output says why.
    A repository already open when the file was written needs reopening.
</p>
